    LLM: 'Game: Ugly. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Ugly is an Australian trick-taking/avoidance game similar to Hearts. 3-4 players, 52-card deck. Players choose trumps each round. Jacks are negative. The 7â™¦ (Ugly Card) doubles Jack penalties OR doubles trick scores if no Jacks captured. The 7â™£ (Charm Card) cancels Ugly's doubling. Card passing escalates each round.",
    objective: 'Accumulate the highest total score over multiple hands; win tricks for +1 point each while avoiding Jacks (negative points) and using the Ugly and Charm cards to modify scoring.',
    gameplay: "Dealer's left picks trump (or no trump). Pass cards (increases each round). Win tricks for +1 pt each. Avoid Jacks (negative). 7â™¦ (Ugly): doubles Jack penalties. 7â™¦ + no Jacks = double trick score. 7â™£ (Charm): cancels Ugly's doubling. Both Ugly+Charm + no Jacks = 4x trick score.",
